></div><div class="dn-review-list"><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="0" data-rating="4" data-size="S" data-fit="false"><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Alex A.</strong> · S<span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="4 out of 5 stars">★★★★☆</span></div><h4>The legs make it</h4><p>Such a funny shape on our dog. Took me a couple of goes to get a picture with all the legs in it, but that was half the fun.</p><details class="dn-review-conversation"><summary>The Dog Nook’s reply</summary><div class="dn-review-reply"><strong>The Dog Nook</strong><p>Thanks, Alex. Fitting all those legs into the picture does sound like part of the entertainment!</p></div></details></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="1" data-rating="4" data-size="M" data-fit="true"><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Beth H.</strong> · M<span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="4 out of 5 stars">★★★★☆</span></div><h4>Glad I checked</h4><p>I nearly ordered by looking at the dog in the photo. Measured ours instead and went for M. Happy with it, though I'd only bought it for a few pictures rather than a whole evening.</p></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="2" data-rating="4" data-size="L" data-fit="false"><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Charlie O.</strong> · L<span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="4 out of 5 stars">★★★★☆</span></div><h4>Funny from the side</h4><p>Love the spider look. The legs disappeared a bit against our dark sofa, so we moved to the kitchen for the photo. Much better there.</p></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="3" data-rating="4" data-size="XL" data-fit="false"><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Dani V.</strong> · XL<span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="4 out of 5 stars">★★★★☆</span></div><h4>Better against a pale wall</h4><p>The black legs don't show up very well against our wallpaper. Against the plain hallway wall it looks great. His face in the middle is the best bit.</p></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="4" data-rating="4" data-size="S" data-fit="true"><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Ellie C.</strong> · S<span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="4 out of 5 stars">★★★★☆</span></div><h4>A little planning helped</h4><p>Bought S after checking the measurements. It worked for our dog, but I wouldn't have wanted to guess. Cute costume once we'd got ourselves organised.</p></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="5" data-rating="5" data-size="M" data-fit="false"><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Fin J.</strong> · M<span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>Not remotely terrifying</h4><p>I thought he might look spooky. He looks like a very pleased little mop with extra legs. We've been laughing at the pictures all evening.</p><details class="dn-review-conversation"><summary>The Dog Nook’s reply</summary><div class="dn-review-reply"><strong>The Dog Nook</strong><p>Fin, “a very pleased little mop” made us smile. Glad the spider turned out to be more funny than frightening.</p></div></details></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="6" data-rating="5" data-size="L" data-fit="false" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Georgie Q.</strong> · L<span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>No hat needed</h4><p>Our dog isn't keen on anything round his ears, so I liked this design straight away. Nothing hiding his face, just a ridiculous spider on his back.</p></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="7" data-rating="3" data-size="S" data-fit="false" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Orla A.</strong> · S<span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="3 out of 5 stars">★★★☆☆</span></div><h4>Marked through the torn bag</h4><p>The parcel had a tear down one side and there was a dusty mark on the spider's body. The costume itself looks funny, but I wanted to check what to do about the mark before trying it on our dog.</p><details class="dn-review-conversation"><summary>View conversation · 2 replies</summary><div class="dn-review-reply"><strong>The Dog Nook</strong><p>Sorry about the torn parcel and the mark, Orla. We can replace the spider costume at no cost. Please send your order number privately so we can confirm the size and sort that out.</p></div><div class="dn-review-reply"><strong>Orla · Follow-up</strong><p>Thanks, the replacement has arrived and this one is clean. Appreciate you sorting it for us.</p></div></details></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="8" data-rating="5" data-size="XL" data-fit="true" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Harper X.</strong> · XL<span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>XL for ours</h4><p>Went for XL using our dog's measurements and it worked for him. The extra legs look particularly funny when he's standing still, looking completely ordinary about it all.</p></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="9" data-rating="5" data-size="S" data-fit="false" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Imogen E.</strong> · S<span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>Mum wants a print</h4><p>Sent Mum a picture of our tiny spider. She's asked for an actual print for the mantelpiece. That says it all really.</p></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="10" data-rating="5" data-size="M" data-fit="false" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Jamie L.</strong> · M<span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>Worth the laugh</h4><p>He sat waiting for his biscuit with those spider legs sticking out either side. Exactly the silly Halloween picture I wanted.</p></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="11" data-rating="5" data-size="L" data-fit="false" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Kit S.</strong> · L<span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>Caught my partner out</h4><p>My partner knew I'd bought a costume but hadn't seen which one. The dog came round the corner and got a proper double take.</p><details class="dn-review-conversation"><summary>The Dog Nook’s reply</summary><div class="dn-review-reply"><strong>The Dog Nook</strong><p>Kit, that entrance sounds perfectly timed. Thanks for telling us about your partner's reaction.</p></div></details></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="12" data-rating="5" data-size="XL" data-fit="false" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Lou Z.</strong> · XL<span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>Big dog, bigger spider</h4><p>Our dog takes XL, so the result wasn't exactly subtle. We put him next to the pumpkin for a picture and the pumpkin suddenly looked rather small.</p></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="13" data-rating="5" data-size="S" data-fit="false" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Morgan G.</strong> · S<span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>Still looks like her</h4><p>That's what I like about it. You can still see our dog's little face and expression, with this completely daft spider shape behind her.</p></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="14" data-rating="5" data-size="M" data-fit="true" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Nicky N.</strong> · M<span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>Good little costume</h4><p>M worked for our dog after measuring. Black spider legs, very serious dog. A winning combination in our house.</p></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="15" data-rating="5" data-size="L" data-fit="true" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Ollie U.</strong> · L<span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>One for the family album</h4><p>We dress up for Halloween most years and finally included the dog in one photo. The spider costume fitted the theme without needing any extra props.</p></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="16" data-rating="5" data-size="XL" data-fit="false" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Pippa B.</strong> · XL<span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>The doorway picture</h4><p>Took a photo from the other end of the hall. You can make out all the legs against the doorway and it looks much funnier than my close-up did.</p><details class="dn-review-conversation"><summary>The Dog Nook’s reply</summary><div class="dn-review-reply"><strong>The Dog Nook</strong><p>Pippa, the doorway sounds like a great backdrop for those legs. Glad you found an angle you liked.</p></div></details></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="17" data-rating="5" data-size="S" data-fit="false" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Quinn I.</strong> · S<span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>Small and silly</h4><p>Bought the small for our dog. It's the contrast between his little real legs and the spider legs that gets me every time.</p></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="18" data-rating="3" data-size="M" data-fit="false" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Reuben F.</strong> · M<span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="3 out of 5 stars">★★★☆☆</span></div><h4>A squashed spider</h4><p>The package arrived very flat and one of the spider legs was caught in the damaged edge of the bag. It had a small tear when I unpacked it. A shame, as the rest looked good.</p><details class="dn-review-conversation"><summary>View conversation · 2 replies</summary><div class="dn-review-reply"><strong>The Dog Nook</strong><p>That's disappointing to find when you open it, Reuben. We'd like to replace the costume free of charge. Could you send us your order number and a photo of that leg privately so we can help?</p></div><div class="dn-review-reply"><strong>Reuben · Follow-up</strong><p>The new spider is here and the legs are all fine. Thank you for replacing it rather than leaving us to mend it.</p></div></details></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="19" data-rating="5" data-size="M" data-fit="false" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Rae P.</strong> · M<span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>The kids chose well</h4><p>I let the children pick between this and a dinosaur. They chose the spider and were delighted when we tried it on him. I think they made the right call.</p></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="20" data-rating="5" data-size="L" data-fit="false" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Sam W.</strong> · L<span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>Not another pumpkin</h4><p>We already have about twenty pumpkin photos. This is a welcome change. The black spider shape looks good with our orange decorations too.</p></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="21" data-rating="5" data-size="XL" data-fit="true" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Taylor D.</strong> · XL<span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>Happy with the size</h4><p>XL was the option that matched our measurements. I was glad we'd checked because I'd initially put L in the basket. It looked right on him when we tried it.</p></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="22" data-rating="5" data-size="S" data-fit="false" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Uma K.</strong> · S<span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>Made my sister jump</h4><p>Only for a second! She spotted the spider legs before she realised it was our dog standing in the hallway. Then she couldn't stop laughing.</p><details class="dn-review-conversation"><summary>The Dog Nook’s reply</summary><div class="dn-review-reply"><strong>The Dog Nook</strong><p>Uma, we can picture that moment of confusion. Glad your sister saw the funny side once she spotted who it was.</p></div></details></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="23" data-rating="5" data-size="M" data-fit="false" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Vicky R.</strong> · M<span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>Straightforward choice</h4><p>Wanted a spider, got a spider. Looks very funny on our dog and I haven't had to buy anything else to go with it.</p></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="24" data-rating="5" data-size="L" data-fit="false" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Will Y.</strong> · L<span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>His ears are the best part</h4><p>His own ears sticking up above the black legs make the whole thing. I wouldn't want a hood covering that face.</p></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="25" data-rating="5" data-size="XL" data-fit="true" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Yasmin F.</strong> · XL<span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>The whole family fits in</h4><p>We had everyone dressed up, including our rather large dog in XL. It's a chaotic family picture, but the spider is very easy to spot.</p></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="26" data-rating="5" data-size="S" data-fit="false" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Zoe M.</strong> · S<span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>Nice against her coat</h4><p>Our dog is pale grey and the black legs stand out really well. I hadn't thought about that when ordering, but the photos came out lovely.</p></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="27" data-rating="5" data-size="M" data-fit="false" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Amelia T.</strong> · M<span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>Now my phone background</h4><p>Just changed my phone background to the dog in his spider costume. Probably keeping it well beyond Halloween.</p><details class="dn-review-conversation"><summary>The Dog Nook’s reply</summary><div class="dn-review-reply"><strong>The Dog Nook</strong><p>Amelia, that's a lovely use for the picture. A spider with a longer season than expected!</p></div></details></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="28" data-rating="5" data-size="L" data-fit="false" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Ben A.</strong> · L<span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>Looks funny sitting down too</h4><p>I thought we'd need a picture of him standing to show it properly. He sat down instead and the legs still made the shape obvious.</p></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="29" data-rating="3" data-size="L" data-fit="false" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Sana K.</strong> · L<span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="3 out of 5 stars">★★★☆☆</span></div><h4>Parcel got wet</h4><p>The outer bag was wet and some moisture had got onto the black body of the costume. Didn't try it on our dog like that. I've sent a message to ask about a replacement.</p><details class="dn-review-conversation"><summary>View conversation · 2 replies</summary><div class="dn-review-reply"><strong>The Dog Nook</strong><p>I'm sorry the moisture reached the costume, Sana. Please leave it unused for now. We can arrange a free replacement; reply privately with your order number and we'll confirm the next step.</p></div><div class="dn-review-reply"><strong>Sana · Follow-up</strong><p>Replacement arrived dry and looks good. Thanks for the help, we've got our spider photo now.</p></div></details></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="30" data-rating="5" data-size="XL" data-fit="false" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Chloe H.</strong> · XL<span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>The one photo we needed</h4><p>Our annual family email needed a Halloween photo. The dog in this was much more entertaining than another picture of our front door decorations.</p></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="31" data-rating="5" data-size="S" data-fit="false" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Dylan O.</strong> · S<span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>Tiny spider face</h4><p>Her little face poking out in front of all those legs is adorable. Very pleased with the small we chose.</p></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="32" data-rating="5" data-size="M" data-fit="false" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Eve V.</strong> · M<span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>Simple idea</h4><p>I preferred this to the costumes with lots of separate bits. The spider shape does enough on its own.</p></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="33" data-rating="5" data-size="L" data-fit="false" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Freddie C.</strong> · L<span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>Even Dad liked it</h4><p>Dad usually rolls his eyes at pet costumes. He asked me to send him the spider picture so he could show someone at work.</p><details class="dn-review-conversation"><summary>The Dog Nook’s reply</summary><div class="dn-review-reply"><strong>The Dog Nook</strong><p>Freddie, getting a photo request from the family sceptic sounds like a success. Thanks for sharing that.</p></div></details></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="34" data-rating="5" data-size="XL" data-fit="false" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><st