iv></details></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="41" data-rating="5" data-size="" data-fit="false" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Isla C.</strong><span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>Easy to recognise in a thumbnail</h4><p>Even when the picture is tiny in our family chat, the skull gives it away. You don't have to zoom in to understand the costume.</p></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="42" data-rating="5" data-size="" data-fit="false" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Jules J.</strong><span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>Right for our photo plans</h4><p>I wanted the dog beside us in our Halloween picture. The dinosaur is obvious enough that he doesn't get lost among the humans' costumes.</p></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="43" data-rating="5" data-size="" data-fit="false" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Lewis Q.</strong><span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>Our usual spot, new look</h4><p>Same armchair in the background, same dog, very different picture. I love how much the skeleton changes an otherwise ordinary scene.</p></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="44" data-rating="5" data-size="" data-fit="false" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Maya X.</strong><span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>No elaborate backdrop</h4><p>We cleared a bit of space and took a photo. The dinosaur skull and spine were enough without the fake cobwebs I'd bought.</p><details class="dn-review-conversation"><summary>The Dog Nook’s reply</summary><div class="dn-review-reply"><strong>The Dog Nook</strong><p>Maya, it sounds like the costume saved you some decorating. Glad the skull and spine did the job on their own.</p></div></details></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="45" data-rating="5" data-size="" data-fit="false" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Noah E.</strong><span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>The profile shot won</h4><p>Printed the side-on picture in the end. You get both his expression and the bones down his back, which is why I chose this costume.</p></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="46" data-rating="5" data-size="" data-fit="false" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Orla L.</strong><span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>Couldn't resist this one</h4><p>Normally I just put the dog next to a pumpkin. Saw the skull on this and decided we could be a bit more ambitious this year.</p></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="47" data-rating="5" data-size="" data-fit="false" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Reuben S.</strong><span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>Good family joke</h4><p>Our dog is afraid of the hoover but apparently can be a dinosaur. The family haven't stopped making jokes about it.</p></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="48" data-rating="5" data-size="" data-fit="false" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Sana Z.</strong><span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>Keeping the photo</h4><p>We only needed the costume for a little while. The picture of that hopeful face underneath the skull is staying on the fridge.</p></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="49" data-rating="5" data-size="" data-fit="false" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Toby G.</strong><span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>Unmistakably a dinosaur</h4><p>The head and the detail along the back work really well together. Several people asked for a second picture from the side.</p><details class="dn-review-conversation"><summary>The Dog Nook’s reply</summary><div class="dn-review-reply"><strong>The Dog Nook</strong><p>Toby, it's lovely that people wanted another angle. Thanks for mentioning how the head and back detail work together.</p></div></details></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="50" data-rating="5" data-size="" data-fit="true" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Esme N.</strong><span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>Glad it suited ours</h4><p>The measurements lined up with our dog and the one-size costume worked for him. Really pleased with the finished look.</p></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="51" data-rating="3" data-size="" data-fit="false" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Morgan V.</strong><span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="3 out of 5 stars">★★★☆☆</span></div><h4>Pale part had a mark</h4><p>The outer packaging had come open and there was a grey mark on the skull section. I could see it in the picture I took, so I didn't want to just ignore it.</p><details class="dn-review-conversation"><summary>View conversation · 2 replies</summary><div class="dn-review-reply"><strong>The Dog Nook</strong><p>I'm sorry it reached you marked, Morgan. We can replace the costume free of charge. Please send the photo and your order number privately so we can confirm the replacement.</p></div><div class="dn-review-reply"><strong>Morgan · Follow-up</strong><p>New costume arrived and the grey mark isn't an issue on this one. Thanks for following it up.</p></div></details></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="52" data-rating="5" data-size="" data-fit="false" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Alex U.</strong><span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>My sister chose well</h4><p>My sister sent me this and said the dog needed it. She was right. We now have a dinosaur picture to embarrass ourselves with at every opportunity.</p></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="53" data-rating="5" data-size="" data-fit="false" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Beth B.</strong><span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>Not another little jumper</h4><p>Wanted something that actually changed the outline of the dog. The skull and the skeleton down the back certainly do that.</p></article><article class="dn-custome