ng><span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>Our daughter's choice</h4><p>Our daughter wanted a dinosaur in the family Halloween photo. This was a much simpler solution than convincing her dad to dress as one.</p></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="58" data-rating="5" data-size="" data-fit="false" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Georgie K.</strong><span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>Funny rather than fierce</h4><p>The teeth should look scary. On our dog, with his usual expression, they really don't. That's why I like it.</p></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="59" data-rating="5" data-size="" data-fit="false" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Harper R.</strong><span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>Would pick it again</h4><p>The skull is fun, the back makes it recognisable, and our dog's face is still the centre of the picture. Happy with our choice.</p></article></div><p data-review-status role="status">Showing 6 of 60 reviews</p><button type="button" class="dn-load-reviews" data-review-more>Load more reviews</button></section>{% endif %}
