en" data-fit="true"><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Sophie E.</strong> · Golden<span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>M suited ours</h4><p>Checked the measurements for M before ordering. It worked for our cat, and the long centipede shape looks wonderfully odd on him.</p></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="4" data-rating="5" data-size="Red" data-fit="false"><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Theo L.</strong> · Red<span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>The red is striking</h4><p>Glad I chose Red. The legs are easy to make out and give the whole thing a properly creepy-crawly look.</p></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="5" data-rating="5" data-size="Golden" data-fit="false"><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Victoria S.</strong> · Golden<span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>Not the usual wings</h4><p>Wanted something different from the bat wings we used last year. The golden-legged centipede is certainly different. We've got a very funny picture now.</p><details class="dn-review-conversation"><summary>The Dog Nook’s reply</summary><div class="dn-review-reply"><strong>The Dog Nook</strong><p>Victoria, it sounds like a definite change from last year's wings. Glad the Golden option gave you a picture you enjoyed.</p></div></details></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="6" data-rating="5" data-size="Red" data-fit="false" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Wren Z.</strong> · Red<span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>My brother laughed first</h4><p>Sent him a picture without saying what it was. His reply was just “why does the cat have so many legs”. Fair question.</p></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="7" data-rating="3" data-size="Red" data-fit="false" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Jade D.</strong> · Red<span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="3 out of 5 stars">★★★☆☆</span></div><h4>Red leg caught in the parcel</h4><p>The bag had been crushed and torn, and one of the red legs had caught in the split. There was a small tear in it when I unpacked the costume. The shape looked fun otherwise.</p><details class="dn-review-conversation"><summary>View conversation · 2 replies</summary><div class="dn-review-reply"><strong>The Dog Nook</strong><p>Sorry about the torn red leg, Jade. We can replace the Red / M costume free of charge. Please send your order number and a photo privately so we can arrange that.</p></div><div class="dn-review-reply"><strong>Jade · Follow-up</strong><p>Thanks, the new red one arrived intact. We've tried it now and got the funny centipede photo we wanted.</p></div></details></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="8" data-rating="5" data-size="Golden" data-fit="false" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Aisha G.</strong> · Golden<span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>Good on a plain floor</h4><p>Tried the golden one on our patterned rug first, then moved to the hallway. You can see the centipede outline much better there.</p></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="9" data-rating="5" data-size="Red" data-fit="false" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Callum N.</strong> · Red<span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>A very strange cat</h4><p>The red legs sticking out along the dark body make him look ridiculous. Exactly what I ordered it for.</p></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="10" data-rating="5" data-size="Golden" data-fit="false" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Elena U.</strong> · Golden<span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>More than a close-up</h4><p>You really need the whole costume in the photograph. The long body is half the joke, so I resisted zooming in on her face for once.</p></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="11" data-rating="5" data-size="Red" data-fit="false" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><strong>Hugo B.</strong> · Red<span class="dn-review-verified">Verified purchase</span></p><span class="dn-review-stars" aria-label="5 out of 5 stars">★★★★★</span></div><h4>Didn't need decorations</h4><p>A plain wall and our cat in the red centipede were enough. I'd got out lots of Halloween bits and ended up putting them away again.</p><details class="dn-review-conversation"><summary>The Dog Nook’s reply</summary><div class="dn-review-reply"><strong>The Dog Nook</strong><p>Hugo, the red centipede sounds like it was doing enough on its own. Glad the simple picture worked for you.</p></div></details></article><article class="dn-customer-review" data-review-item data-review-order="12" data-rating="5" data-size="Golden" data-fit="false" hidden><div class="dn-review-card-head"><p class="dn-review-author"><str